# 005-switchpt-two-versions: PumpAi SwitchPT scores the host as two creatures (forge-ai CODE patch, NOT applied; needs approval)
# What: for `AILogic$ SwitchPT` on the host itself (PumpAi.checkAiLogic) the AI now (1) only considers it in declare blockers
# of a combat the host is in (checkPhaseRestrictions), (2) scores the host "as it is now" (P/T) and "switched" (T/P) in this
# combat (unblocked attacker: damage, lethal = 10000; blocked attacker / blocker: value of the opposing creatures it kills,
# cheapest first, minus its own value if it dies) and switches only if the other version scores higher, (3) allows at most
# one switch and one switch back per turn. Idea from the user: view the switch as a temporary second creature and pick the
# more useful version for the rest of the turn.
# Cards affected: Aquamoeba, Turtleshell Changeling, Myr Quadropod, and any other self SwitchPT card (needs patch 001 for the
# flags). Test (AiLabSim, n001 deck 40 cards, equal life 20, 10 games, vs Sai deck):
#   001 flag removal only:   casts 20ish, ~92 activations/10 games (58 with the creature not in combat; none helped)
#   guard v1 (simple rules): casts 20, 4 activations, all in declare blockers
#   this patch (two-version scoring): casts 13, 8 activations, all in declare blockers; sample: unblocked Myr Quadropod
#   switched to 4 power (+2 damage); Aquamoeba traded with a Thopter Mechanic.
# Not modelled: first strike/deathtouch, combat tricks, switching a blocker before blocks. Apply: git apply this file on forge-ai.
diff --git a/forge-ai/src/main/java/forge/ai/ability/PumpAi.java b/forge-ai/src/main/java/forge/ai/ability/PumpAi.java
